WHY THIS LICENSE EXISTS
-----------------------

This software runs security-critical infrastructure. Its entire value rests on a
promise: that the system does exactly what it says it does, and nothing else. A
promise like that is worthless if you have to take our word for it. So we are
giving you the means to check.

You may read every line of this source code. You may build it yourself. You may
run it to confirm it behaves as described, and you may reproduce our results
independently. If our claims are true, you can verify that they are true — from
the source, without asking us, without trusting us. That transparency is the
point, and it is why this code is open for you to inspect.

This is not open-source software, and we are honest about the one thing we hold
back: our patents. We invented the methods this software embodies, and we keep
the patent rights to them. We use those rights defensively — to stop this work
from being copied, forked, or reimplemented into a competing product.

You are free to look, learn, build, and verify. You are also free to run the
official images we publish to cloud providers (AWS, GCP, Azure, and others) —
exactly as we make them available — for any purpose, including production. That
is the product. The attested image is the distribution channel; the attestation
guarantee is what you are paying for. Running our published images does not
require a separate patent license.

What you may not do is take the patented inventions — the methods, the
architecture, the attestation model — and reimplement them, fork them into a
competing product, or build your own distribution that bypasses ours. We protect
against forks not because we fear competition in the abstract, but because the
attestation model depends on the integrity of the images we publish. A forked
image that claims to be "Safebox-compatible" but runs modified code breaks the
promise that end users rely on. Our patent rights exist to protect that promise.

That is the whole bargain, in one sentence: a fully transparent, independently
verifiable codebase, distributed as attested cloud images you can run freely,
with the patents reserved so the system's integrity guarantee cannot be forked
away. Inspect and verify all you like. Run our images all you like. Practicing
the patented inventions outside our published images takes our permission.

End users are free to interact with software running inside a Safebox — through
its APIs, its streams, its tools, its web interfaces — in any way the software
permits. The running system's own rules govern what is allowed: what actions
require approval, what data can be accessed, what tools can execute. Code is
law, the same principle that governs smart contracts on a blockchain.

Developers are free to write applications that communicate with a Safebox from
the outside — clients, integrations, bots, dashboards — without any license
from us. Your application talks to the Safebox; the Safebox enforces its own
policies. That boundary is clean.

If you want to install your own software inside a Safebox — to run a custom
application that benefits from the attested environment, the governance engine,
the sealed credential vault, and all the guarantees the platform provides —
you may do so through the mechanisms the software itself provides (app layers,
plugins, tools), subject to the software's own approval process. If you need
a custom flavor of Safebox with software installed outside those mechanisms,
or if you want to distribute your own Safebox images that include your
proprietary software under the attestation umbrella, contact us for a custom
license.

The formal terms follow. Where the plain-language explanation above and the
formal terms below differ, the formal terms govern.


