"Non-Production Use" means using the Licensed Work for any of the following, and
nothing beyond them: reading and studying the source code; building and
compiling it; running it to inspect, test, evaluate, audit, or independently
verify its behavior or reproduce its results; security research; education and
teaching; and experimentation and development. Non-Production Use is use to
LEARN ABOUT and CHECK the Licensed Work — not to operate a live service or
product for others, and not to process other people's data as part of running a
business.

"Production Use" means any use that is not Non-Production Use. This includes,
without limitation: operating the Licensed Work (or anything derived from it) to
provide a service or product to any third party; using it to process third-party
data as part of a commercial or operational offering; and using it in, or as
part of, any product or service that competes with any product or service we
offer.

"Authorized Deployment" means running an unmodified machine image or container
image that we have published and made available through a supported cloud
provider (such as AWS, GCP, or Azure) or through our own distribution channels,
where the image's integrity is verifiable through the attestation mechanisms
described in the Licensed Work. Authorized Deployment is permitted for any
purpose, including Production Use, without a separate patent license, because
the integrity guarantee that our patents protect is preserved by the unmodified
image. An image is "unmodified" if it passes the attestation verification
procedures included in the Licensed Work.

"External Interaction" means communicating with a running instance of the
Licensed Work from outside it — through its published APIs, protocols, web
interfaces, stream subscriptions, tool invocations, or any other interface the
running software exposes. External Interaction includes writing and operating
client applications, integrations, bots, dashboards, and other software that
communicates with the Licensed Work over a network. External Interaction does
not require any license from us — your software talks to the Safebox; the
Safebox's own rules govern what it permits.

"In-Safebox Installation" means installing your own software inside a running
instance of the Licensed Work, through the mechanisms the software itself
provides: app layers, plugins, tools, or any other installation mechanism that
the governance and attestation systems are designed to accommodate. In-Safebox
Installation is permitted without a separate license from us, subject to the
running software's own approval process (governance policies, app-layer
attestation, M-of-N blessing where required). Software installed through these
mechanisms operates under the Safebox's rules — code is law.

"Custom Image Distribution" means creating, modifying, or distributing machine
images or container images that include the Licensed Work (or parts of it)
combined with your own software, outside the mechanisms the Licensed Work
provides for In-Safebox Installation. Custom Image Distribution requires a
separate written license from us.

"Patent Claims" means any claims of any patent or patent application, now
existing or later arising, that we own or control, that are or would be
infringed by making, using, selling, offering to sell, importing, running, or
otherwise practicing the Licensed Work or any method, technique, or invention it
embodies.


